# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit. A leaked token here means anyone on the machine can
# drive a logged-in ERP session; a leaked connections.json means database
# credentials. Both are listed first because both are unrecoverable once pushed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
secret.txt
**/agent/drive/
connections.json
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output — the agent jar is rebuilt on every run by design (a stale jar
# is the single most confusing failure mode this project has), so it must never
# be committed or reused.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.jar
*.class
classes/
manifest.txt
javac.log
attach.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local run artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.out
*_log.txt
o2c_state.json
.ebs/

# Ad-hoc scratch scripts. Exploratory one-offs accumulate fast while working a
# new form; they capture a moment, not a method, and are noise in a repo.
_*.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
